1
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:24,460
We sigh whenever we're about to come to a standstill

2
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:24,460
Owarinaki tabi no tochuu tachidomarisouna toki

3
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,710
While moving on this endless journey.

4
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,710
Fukai tameiki kobosu bokura wa

5
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,430
Everytime we lunge for it, it escapes and flies off.

6
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,430
Tsukamikaketewa mata hanareteitta

7
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:45,850
But now, there's nothing to be afraid of

8
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:45,850
Demo ima wa mou nanimo osoreru koto wa nai

9
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,780
The powerful ties that bind our hearts

10
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,780
Kokoro wo tsunagu tsuyoi kizuna wa

11
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:59,240
Will never come loose.

12
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:59,240
Keshite hodoke wa shinai sa

13
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:08,960
After a lifetime of searching, we finally arrived

14
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:08,960
Sagashitsuzukete tadoritsuita

15
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:14,760
Here, where the period lies.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:14,760
Kono basho de piriodo ni

17
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:24,060
Let's change all our sorrow and rage to power.

18
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:24,060
Kanashimi ikari chikara ni kaete

19
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,980
Destiny is right within our reach.

20
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,980
Unmei wa sugu soba ni

21
00:01:50,330 --> 00:01:53,130
It's that expression again, May.

22
00:01:53,130 --> 00:01:56,300
Yeah, that also represents gold.

23
00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:57,720
What are you two doing?

24
00:01:59,470 --> 00:02:02,640
We're checking to see whether there's a hidden message here.

25
00:02:03,050 --> 00:02:04,220
A hidden message?

26
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:12,560
Alchemists often hide their research using trope and hidden meanings to prevent ordinary people from deciphering it.

27
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:16,320
But at a glance, these documents aren't encrypted.

28
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:24,330
So we're going to note that phrases with "immortality" and "gold" appear quite often to try to view things differently.

29
00:02:24,330 --> 00:02:26,620
Think you're on to something then?

30
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:28,080
Not at all.

31
00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:32,330
Where am I?

32
00:02:32,330 --> 00:02:33,130
Al!

33
00:02:33,130 --> 00:02:33,880
Sir Al!

34
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:35,170
I'm so glad!

35
00:02:35,170 --> 00:02:38,590
I was worried you'd never wake up!

36
00:02:39,170 --> 00:02:41,880
Sorry for worrying all of you.

37
00:02:42,590 --> 00:02:46,010
So, why am I in pieces?

38
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:49,640
And that's where we're at now.

39
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:54,020
You were too large to carry.

40
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:56,020
That is why we had to take you apart.

41
00:02:56,440 --> 00:03:00,530
Sorry to give you guys so much trouble.

42
00:03:00,530 --> 00:03:02,910
Has this ever happened before?

43
00:03:02,910 --> 00:03:06,160
Just once, while I was on my way here.

44
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:12,870
It must be inconvenient for you to be scattered in pieces.

45
00:03:12,870 --> 00:03:15,170
Let's put you back together.

46
00:03:15,170 --> 00:03:17,300
Thanks, I appreciate it.

47
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:19,630
Could you hold on to this for a second?

48
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:23,260
Let's see...

49
00:03:25,010 --> 00:03:26,350
This is...

50
00:03:26,350 --> 00:03:28,560
I think that's his right arm.

51
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:32,560
Ah, you're right. We have to put him back together properly.

52
00:03:35,150 --> 00:03:36,310
Scattered in pieces...

53
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:39,030
Putting things together...

54
00:03:50,750 --> 00:03:52,250
Hey, May?!

55
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,420
Look at what you've done!

56
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:56,960
They're all scattered now!

57
00:04:01,050 --> 00:04:02,880
I was wondering...

58
00:04:04,090 --> 00:04:10,180
...how it would look if we changed the pages' order by grouping terms such as "gold" and "immortality".

59
00:04:16,850 --> 00:04:20,690
"Golden Being"... I saw that term over there.

60
00:04:20,690 --> 00:04:23,860
"Immortality"... overlaps with these right here.

61
00:04:24,650 --> 00:04:26,610
"Perfect Being"...

62
00:04:26,610 --> 00:04:27,950
Ah, I found it!

63
00:04:28,410 --> 00:04:30,490
Hand me those pages, Marcoh.

64
00:04:30,490 --> 00:04:32,500
Oh, that ties into these!

65
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:34,000
Does anyone have a "Golden Being"?

66
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,710
I do. It's right here.

67
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:41,550
That should be the last of them.

68
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:49,720
Could it be...

69
00:04:57,940 --> 00:04:58,810
This is...

70
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:04,990
The Nationwide Transmutation Circle...

71
00:05:05,990 --> 00:05:09,030
Even if we find out about this now...

72
00:05:09,030 --> 00:05:10,700
What does this mean?

73
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:13,330
Do you mean these research documents won't be of any use at all?!

74
00:05:13,330 --> 00:05:15,450
You've gotta be kidding me!

75
00:05:15,450 --> 00:05:16,290
What's going to happen to us-

76
00:05:16,290 --> 00:05:16,960
No...

77
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:18,580
What's going to happen to this country?!

78
00:05:19,330 --> 00:05:21,000
I apologize...

79
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:27,840
I was foolish to hope someone else's studies would overturn this crisis.

80
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:35,520
Brother, is this what you wanted to tell me?

81
00:05:36,430 --> 00:05:41,400
Knowing you, shouldn't you have gotten further than this?

82
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:44,650
There's still something else.

83
00:05:46,570 --> 00:05:49,030
We didn't even realize to take it apart at first.

84
00:05:49,030 --> 00:05:53,530
It wouldn't be strange if there was more hidden in these documents!

85
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:56,830
Yeah.

86
00:06:05,630 --> 00:06:07,720
Idiot! What were you thinking?!

87
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:10,010
It's Mother Nature's fault for making it so cold.

88
00:06:10,010 --> 00:06:12,300
Besides, I'm sensitive to the cold!

89
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:13,100
So what?!

90
00:06:14,390 --> 00:06:17,680
Now we don't know front from back!

91
00:06:20,350 --> 00:06:23,400
Look at all these you flipped over!

92
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:24,480
That may be it!

93
00:06:25,230 --> 00:06:28,360
We need to "overturn" this crisis!

94
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:32,660
Flip each one of them over from how they were originally!

95
00:06:41,870 --> 00:06:42,710
Well?

96
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:44,920
Bingo.

97
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:53,430
This is a new Amestrian Nationwide Transmutation Circle that is activated when Eastern Alchemy is made a part of it.

98
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:57,200
Signs of a 
Counteroffensive

99
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:57,200
Signs of a 
Counteroffensive

100
00:07:09,280 --> 00:07:12,660
I don't see any signs of them going this way.

101
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:16,870
Perhaps I took a wrong turn somewhere. I guess I'll go back.

102
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:54,200
I see.

103
00:07:54,740 --> 00:08:00,830
So this place is used to remove the rubble from the tunnel Sloth is digging.

104
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:07,500
You're the Crimson Alchemist, correct?

105
00:08:08,170 --> 00:08:11,630
Pleasure to meet you. I'm Pride.

106
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:14,720
Can I help you?

107
00:08:15,470 --> 00:08:17,970
What happened with Scar?

108
00:08:17,970 --> 00:08:20,180
I'm currently after him.

109
00:08:20,180 --> 00:08:21,720
Save that for later.

110
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:25,730
First, carve a bloody crest into Briggs.

111
00:08:25,730 --> 00:08:31,860
With all due respect, the soldiers at Briggs are quite monolithic and powerful.

112
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:34,650
It won't be that easy.

113
00:08:34,650 --> 00:08:37,450
You need to utilize that exact strength.

114
00:08:41,830 --> 00:08:45,920
The tunnel being dug by Sloth is almost complete.

115
00:08:47,750 --> 00:08:49,630
I understand.

116
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:52,670
As you say, I'll carve a bloody crest.

117
00:08:53,210 --> 00:08:55,470
To the Briggs fortress.

118
00:09:08,900 --> 00:09:10,650
We've been waiting for you!

119
00:09:11,190 --> 00:09:12,520
Any changes?

120
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:14,400
Nothing in particular.

121
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:18,740
Moving right on, I heard Kimblee has gone missing. Is this true?

122
00:09:18,740 --> 00:09:20,070
Yes.

123
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:23,540
There was an explosion large enough to cause a shaft to collapse.

124
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:26,460
Kimblee and a few others are missing.

125
00:09:26,460 --> 00:09:30,380
We searched the rubble, but in the end, found no bodies.

126
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:35,300
Are the "few others" soldiers from Briggs?

127
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:38,680
No.

128
00:09:38,680 --> 00:09:40,640
Two of Kimblee's men...

129
00:09:42,350 --> 00:09:44,010
...and the Fullmetal Alchemist.

130
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:52,310
Oh. The Fullmetal boss, eh?

131
00:09:53,070 --> 00:09:54,570
I hope he's okay.

132
00:09:54,570 --> 00:09:55,530
As do I.

133
00:09:56,860 --> 00:09:58,150
How are things in the west?

134
00:09:59,150 --> 00:10:03,580
Things are getting nasty on the Pendleton border.

135
00:10:04,370 --> 00:10:08,120
From their way of fighting, I can't help but think they're trying  to produce more deaths.

136
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:15,590
As you said, it seems like the army is taking the initiative in causing bloodshed to create a transmutation circle.

137
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:19,590
Have you gotten word from
Master Sergeant Fuery in the south?

138
00:10:20,220 --> 00:10:23,100
He called me a little while ago.

139
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:27,810
He says they're having an all-out war with the Aerugon army in South Fotsett.

140
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:46,700
R... Run, Thomas!

141
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:47,790
No time to rest!

142
00:10:47,790 --> 00:10:48,620
Thoma-

143
00:10:55,420 --> 00:10:57,630
Dammit!

144
00:10:57,630 --> 00:10:58,960
I will survive!

145
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:01,880
God dammit, I will  survive!!

146
00:11:06,060 --> 00:11:07,390
I see.

147
00:11:08,180 --> 00:11:12,270
After all, we, members of Mustang's old team, aren't so popular.

148
00:11:13,350 --> 00:11:15,270
Have you been in contact with the Colonel?

149
00:11:15,270 --> 00:11:20,030
Yes, in full detail. We've been using a messenger who's acquainted with the Armstrong family.

150
00:11:22,150 --> 00:11:23,410
Roger that.

151
00:11:23,410 --> 00:11:25,910
Things seem to be getting pretty serious up north, so be careful.

152
00:11:26,530 --> 00:11:28,990
Serious sounds about right.

153
00:11:30,330 --> 00:11:36,040
The underlings of the man who's planning to turn this country into Hell are proceeding steadily with their plan,

154
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:38,750
but there's not a single thing we can do about it.

155
00:11:51,310 --> 00:11:53,390
It's connected.

156
00:11:54,900 --> 00:12:00,280
I don't have to work anymore... right... Pride?

157
00:12:04,450 --> 00:12:06,490
The time is near.

158
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:10,990
The day is right within our reach.

159
00:12:27,890 --> 00:12:29,600
Guys!

160
00:12:30,810 --> 00:12:34,140
Lunch is served! Please line up!

161
00:12:38,020 --> 00:12:42,030
Hey Rose, I'd like to have meat pie next time.

162
00:12:42,030 --> 00:12:44,450
We'll make some if we get the ingredients.

163
00:12:44,450 --> 00:12:46,160
I'll be looking forward to it!

164
00:12:47,410 --> 00:12:54,290
I don't work here, but do you think you could possibly give these two something to eat?

165
00:12:54,910 --> 00:12:56,670
Why not?

166
00:12:56,670 --> 00:12:58,040
There's plenty for you, too, madam.

167
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:04,170
This looks so good!

168
00:13:04,170 --> 00:13:06,180
Can I get an extra scoop, Rose?

169
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:10,300
Sorry, everyone gets the same amount.

170
00:13:10,300 --> 00:13:13,180
Excuse me...

171
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:17,560
C-Can I have some, as well?

172
00:13:23,230 --> 00:13:25,400
You saved me!

173
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:27,740
Thank you so much. It was great.

174
00:13:27,740 --> 00:13:30,660
Where did you come from?

175
00:13:30,660 --> 00:13:34,580
That's a difficult question to answer,
since I've been wandering all over the place.

176
00:13:36,080 --> 00:13:38,620
But why Lior of all places?

177
00:13:38,620 --> 00:13:42,250
You've heard of the riot that happened here, right?

178
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:47,380
There's nothing left in this town because of it.

179
00:13:49,430 --> 00:13:52,510
There are delicious meals here, are there not?

180
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:58,350
I'm flattered by your compliment,

181
00:13:59,390 --> 00:14:02,770
but this is about all I can do to help.

182
00:14:02,770 --> 00:14:04,400
That's not true.

183
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:10,570
Both the warm meals you serve and the bright smile on your face motivate everyone to work.

184
00:14:15,620 --> 00:14:16,790
That's right.

185
00:14:17,330 --> 00:14:22,710
I know you just saved my life,
but I'm actually looking for a church.

186
00:14:23,630 --> 00:14:24,630
A church?

187
00:14:24,630 --> 00:14:29,630
Yeah. The headquarters of the Leto religion, the cause of the riot.

188
00:14:38,810 --> 00:14:40,770
It's just as you see.

189
00:14:40,770 --> 00:14:42,900
Even if you go in, there won't be anything left.

190
00:14:43,650 --> 00:14:46,360
Is there a passage that leads underground?

191
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:49,700
Y-Yes, there is, but...

192
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:56,490
What's this?

193
00:14:56,490 --> 00:14:58,200
A poisoned reservoir.

194
00:14:58,200 --> 00:15:00,500
It was already like that when we found it.

195
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:10,510
So an ordinary human won't be able to get past this.

196
00:15:11,050 --> 00:15:11,760
Let's see.

197
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:12,510
Wait!

198
00:15:12,510 --> 00:15:13,720
You'll die if you step in it!

199
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:24,100
A miracle...

200
00:15:24,810 --> 00:15:29,320
You mean... alchemy...

201
00:15:30,570 --> 00:15:34,620
I'm going to go a bit further,
so could you wait for me here?

202
00:15:50,050 --> 00:15:51,880
Wow...

203
00:15:53,630 --> 00:15:55,390
This place is huge.

204
00:15:55,390 --> 00:15:59,510
Damn him, making something so large.

205
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:06,650
That was quick.

206
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:27,830
Uh oh, that wasn't even enough to slow you down.

207
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:29,380
In that case...

208
00:16:30,630 --> 00:16:33,010
Why don't I trap you?!

209
00:16:39,260 --> 00:16:40,680
Uh oh...

210
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:47,560
This isn't good...

211
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:08,000
What's wrong? Aren't you going to kill me?

212
00:17:08,710 --> 00:17:09,750
Hmm?

213
00:17:10,460 --> 00:17:14,260
You... You're Van Hohenheim, aren't you?

214
00:17:15,550 --> 00:17:18,760
Looks like this is as far as you can go.

215
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:24,270
You'll die if you go any further?

216
00:17:25,730 --> 00:17:28,980
Going past this line will result in your death, right?

217
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:32,020
Kind of like that flask.

218
00:17:34,610 --> 00:17:39,410
So, my conclusion is you can only move within this tunnel and in the center portion of Central.

219
00:17:39,410 --> 00:17:40,700
What do you say?

220
00:17:42,700 --> 00:17:44,080
Am I right?

221
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:51,250
What's wrong? Why don't you say something, Mr. Can't-Leave-His-Home?!

222
00:17:54,670 --> 00:17:56,170
You mad?

223
00:17:56,880 --> 00:18:00,640
There's no such thing as wrath within me.

224
00:18:02,600 --> 00:18:04,890
Not just wrath.

225
00:18:04,890 --> 00:18:08,690
I left all of my unnecessary emotions within Father.

226
00:18:08,690 --> 00:18:11,520
My name is Pride.

227
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:13,730
Pride...

228
00:18:13,730 --> 00:18:16,280
I see, so that stands for "avarice".

229
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:22,280
They say man is embodied by seven deadly sins.

230
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:24,160
Lust.

231
00:18:24,790 --> 00:18:26,040
Greed.

232
00:18:26,580 --> 00:18:27,910
Sloth.

233
00:18:28,460 --> 00:18:29,410
Gluttony.

234
00:18:30,370 --> 00:18:31,670
Envy.

235
00:18:32,330 --> 00:18:33,630
Wrath.

236
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:37,670
And... Pride.

237
00:18:39,220 --> 00:18:44,390
So the emotion he let go of first was you. "Pride".

238
00:18:45,390 --> 00:18:50,440
Funny how he detached you to look exactly as he did when he was in the flask.

239
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:58,360
So that appearance itself is the true nature of that arrogant, self-adulating father of yours.

240
00:18:59,570 --> 00:19:02,490
I'm going to ask that you visit my father.

241
00:19:02,950 --> 00:19:05,280
Hey, no need to rush things.

242
00:19:05,280 --> 00:19:07,540
Don't worry; I'd visit him even if I weren't invited.

243
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:11,000
Tell him this:

244
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:14,290
"Slave Number 23 will be coming to see you soon."

245
00:19:16,170 --> 00:19:20,420
"Throw yourself back in your chair in Central while you wait for him."

246
00:19:20,420 --> 00:19:21,300
Got it?

247
00:19:23,640 --> 00:19:25,970
Sure, I'll be waiting for you.

248
00:19:26,560 --> 00:19:29,470
Van Hohenheim.

249
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:42,950
He's back.

250
00:19:46,160 --> 00:19:47,740
Find anything?

251
00:19:47,740 --> 00:19:49,120
Yeah...

252
00:19:49,120 --> 00:19:53,000
People shouldn't go near this place. It's dangerous.

253
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:55,540
Please tell everyone not to go in.

254
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:03,720
What were you doing down there?

255
00:20:07,050 --> 00:20:09,850
Just a little declaration of war.

256
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:15,150
Your shift is up.

257
00:20:15,150 --> 00:20:19,360
Finally! The blizzard was killing me!

258
00:20:19,770 --> 00:20:23,780
I guess I'll go have a cup of bad coffee.

259
00:20:23,780 --> 00:20:25,200
Good work.

260
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:34,080
H-Hey!

261
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:36,290
Don't tell me that's...

262
00:20:38,750 --> 00:20:40,210
The Drakman army?!

263
00:20:43,590 --> 00:20:46,430
Drakma to the north has declared open hostilities!

264
00:20:46,430 --> 00:20:48,430
All men, battle positions!

265
00:20:48,430 --> 00:20:49,390
I repeat!

266
00:20:49,390 --> 00:20:52,060
Drakma to the north has declared open hostilities!

267
00:20:52,060 --> 00:20:54,180
All men, battle positions!

268
00:21:08,740 --> 00:21:13,160
We're lucky the Northern Wall of Briggs isn't around.

269
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:15,750
Right, Sir Kimblee?

270
00:21:15,750 --> 00:21:21,710
Additionally, there are many men loyal to me in the fort.

271
00:21:21,710 --> 00:21:27,260
Once the battle begins, they'll betray the others, causing the fort to be thrown into confusion.

272
00:21:28,930 --> 00:21:33,520
At last, I shall take Briggs by storm.

273
00:21:34,020 --> 00:21:36,520
The fort that has stood in the way of Drakma for eternity!

274
00:21:36,520 --> 00:21:39,900
It's time for the declaration of war.

275
00:21:40,730 --> 00:21:43,820
Let's launch some fireworks, shall we?!

276
00:21:44,280 --> 00:21:46,700
All cannons at the ready!

277
00:21:56,370 --> 00:21:57,580
Fire!!!

278
00:22:15,310 --> 00:22:20,270
The promise we never made

279
00:22:15,310 --> 00:22:20,270
Kawashita hazu no nai yakasoku ga

280
00:22:20,270 --> 00:22:21,060
yet again

281
00:22:20,270 --> 00:22:21,060
Kyou mo

282
00:22:21,060 --> 00:22:25,900
tries to snatch our future away from us.

283
00:22:21,060 --> 00:22:25,900
Bokura no mirai wo ubaou to suru

284
00:22:27,530 --> 00:22:31,490
Why is it that we can't rejoice

285
00:22:27,530 --> 00:22:31,490
Hoshigatteita mono wo te ni shitemo

286
00:22:31,490 --> 00:22:32,490
straight from the heart

287
00:22:31,490 --> 00:22:32,490
Sunao ni

288
00:22:32,490 --> 00:22:37,450
when we obtain something we've always been after?

289
00:22:32,490 --> 00:22:37,450
Umaku waraenai nowa nazedarou

290
00:22:38,120 --> 00:22:43,170
The overflowing tears aren't from feebleness or remorse.

291
00:22:38,120 --> 00:22:43,170
Afureru namida wo yowasa ya koukai ja nai

292
00:22:43,840 --> 00:22:47,960
They're fragments born from agony.

293
00:22:43,840 --> 00:22:47,960
Itami ga unda kakera de

294
00:22:49,630 --> 00:22:53,010
Of all the moments and destinies,

295
00:22:49,630 --> 00:22:53,010
Donna shunkan datte unmei datte

296
00:22:53,010 --> 00:23:01,770
I realized there's one absolute certainty.

297
00:22:53,010 --> 00:23:01,770
Hitotsu dake tashika na mono ga aru to shitta

298
00:23:01,770 --> 00:23:04,310
Even if things get tough and I'm at my limit

299
00:23:01,770 --> 00:23:04,310
Genkai datte konnan datte

300
00:23:04,310 --> 00:23:08,320
I refuse to give up.

301
00:23:04,310 --> 00:23:08,320
Akirametakunaiyo

302
00:23:08,320 --> 00:23:13,200
Please, don't let go.

303
00:23:08,320 --> 00:23:13,200
Konomama hanasanaide

304
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:21,040
I can feel the warmth of your right hand

305
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:21,040
Kataku nigirishimeta kimi no migite no nukumori

306
00:23:21,040 --> 00:23:24,710
where it's tightly joined with my left.

307
00:23:21,040 --> 00:23:24,710
Koko ni arukara

308
00:23:33,340 --> 00:23:36,300
Yeah, that's right. My name is Zampano.

309
00:23:36,810 --> 00:23:37,930
One of Kimblee's men.

310
00:23:38,560 --> 00:23:42,190
Doctor Marcoh is currently hiding in the slums of Asbec.

311
00:23:42,770 --> 00:23:45,730
I appreciate you telling us, Zampano.

312
00:23:45,730 --> 00:23:47,820
We'll guarantee your safety.

313
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:53,610
Marcoh!

314
00:23:55,450 --> 00:23:57,490
Things are getting interesting!

315
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:03,000
Wily souls bring about a catastrophe,

316
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:06,670
and the pride making the decision gets hurt in the process.

317
00:24:07,040 --> 00:24:11,380
But it's inevitable in the process of rebirth.

318
00:24:12,470 --> 00:24:16,850
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

319
00:24:16,850 --> 00:24:20,870
Episode 43, Bite of the Ant.

320
00:24:16,870 --> 00:24:20,870
Bite of the Ant

321
00:24:21,430 --> 00:24:23,390
The snowfield is dyed red.

322
00:24:24,190 --> 00:24:27,230
The color of blood that was shed to protect.
